    },
    {
     "label": "1972 Nixon opening",
     "note": "The story begins with Nixon's trip to Beijing and the long bet that engagement would shape Chinese behavior. Under this opening, the current reframing is one more swing in a fifty-year cycle of opening, integration and pullback between two powers that have always managed each other as peers in practice. This is the frame realist historians, Russian and Chinese state outlets and many European analysts open with."
